WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Hey, welcome back to Tesla Short's Time Daily, episode 436.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.620
It's April 14th, 2026, and I'm Patrick here in Vancouver.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.660
Grab a coffee if you're just waking up.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:12.440
We've got a full slate today that touches on software

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:15.940
that actually feels useful, regulatory movement in Europe,

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.840
what's happening inside the factories,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.140
and some bigger picture thinking about

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.340
where Tesla fits in price-sensitive markets.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:23.820
Let's get into it.

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.760
The spring 2026 software update is starting to roll out

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.140
and the headline feature that's getting the most immediate

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.500
attention is the voice-activated GROC assistant.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.400
Tesla has now enabled hands-free voice activation,

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.500
so instead of having to glance down at the screen

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:38.460
or tap anything, drivers can just say,

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.180
hey, GROC and the AI is right there.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.380
It's a small-sounding change,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.640
but I think it's actually pretty meaningful for safety.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.440
Keeping your eyes on the road,

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.320
while still being able to ask for navigation changes,

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.260
play a podcast, adjust climate,

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.460
or even get a joke from GROC removes one of those little friction

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.040
points that used to pull attention away from driving.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.500
Tesla has been methodically moving in-car AI

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:03.040
toward something that feels natural rather than bolted on.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:06.100
For a long time, the voice systems in most cars,

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.980
not just Tesla, felt like an afterthought

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.500
that you had to baby a bit.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:12.600
This update feels like the moment

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.380
where it starts crossing over into,

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.740
I don't even think about it anymore territory.

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.640
And because it's coming over the air,

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:21.600
a huge installed base is going to wake up to it

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.540
in the next few weeks.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:24.660
From a product-experienced standpoint,

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.600
it quietly raises the bar on what people expect

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.800
from an intelligent car.

00:01:29.380 --> 00:01:33.000
It also sets the stage nicely for the bigger autonomy conversation

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.760
because the same voice layer that now feels effortless

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.020
is eventually going to be the primary interface

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:40.200
once the car is doing more of the actual driving.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.480
Speaking of which, Dutch authorities

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.880
have formally approved Tesla's full self-driving software.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:49.280
That regulatory green light means the supervised version

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.560
can now be activated for customers in the Netherlands

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:53.040
without the previous restrictions.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.820
It's one of those incremental but important steps

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.660
that removes a barrier in a very mature EV market

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.420
where regulators have historically moved cautiously.

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.440
For Tesla's European business, this is helpful

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.340
because it makes the car's more attractive

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.400
to fleet buyers and private customers

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.900
who want the latest features.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.240
Deliveries in Europe have been a bit lumpy at times,

00:02:13.480 --> 00:02:15.480
so clearing regulatory hurdles like this

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.820
tends to smooth things out

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:19.260
and gives salespeople a clearer story to tell.

00:02:19.660 --> 00:02:22.360
I'm trying not to over-hype any single approval, though.

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:25.940
Europe's road rules vary country by country, cities are dense,

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:29.060
and the cultural comfort level with autonomous systems

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:29.960
is still evolving.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:32.600
So while this is clearly positive,

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.280
the real test remains how quickly Tesla can move

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.040
from supervised to unsupervised driving at scale,

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.180
and whether the system can handle the unpredictable mix

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.380
of bicycles, trams, and aggressive merging

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:47.200
you see in places like Amsterdam or Rotterdam.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:48.880
Still, it's another data point

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.860
that the regulatory side of autonomy

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:53.300
isn't completely stalled on its inching forward,

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:56.360
even if the bigger scaling challenges are still ahead of us.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.120
While Europe inches forward on the software side,

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.120
Tesla's manufacturing machine in China

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:02.920
is quietly doing what it does best,

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.400
pumping out more vehicles.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:07.340
Deliveries coming out of the Shanghai Gigafactory

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:08.320
have ramped up again.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:11.680
That plant has always been a dual-purpose operation.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.140
It feeds the huge domestic Chinese market

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.400
while also producing cars for export to Europe, Australia,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.180
and other right-hand drive markets.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:21.300
The increased output underscores

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.500
just how central Shanghai has become

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:25.680
to Tesla's overall volume strategy

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:27.680
when regional demand shifts

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.360
or when new competitors pop up

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.900
having that flexible, high-efficiency factory

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.060
gives Tesla real breathing room.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.300
I've always been impressed by how quickly

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:39.080
the team in Shanghai iterates on production lines.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:41.160
The manufacturing efficiency there

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.980
continues to be one of Tesla's

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:44.580
clearest competitive advantages,

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.000
lower costs, high output, and the ability

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.880
to tweak models for local tastes

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:53.020
without retooling an entire continent's worth of factories.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.980
In a year where global EV growth has been uneven,

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.340
that steady increase in Shanghai shipments

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:00.460
is one of the more reliable pieces of the puzzle.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:02.920
It helps balance supply across continents

00:04:02.920 --> 00:04:05.120
and keeps the overall company at a scale

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.580
that smaller players simply can't match right now.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:10.360
And that idea of expanding reach

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:12.320
brings us naturally to India.

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.580
Tesla appears set to introduce a new product there

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.980
on April 22nd.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:19.260
The speculation has been pretty consistent.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:20.840
Most people think we're looking

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.020
at a more affordable version of the Model 3,

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.320
though there's always the chance

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:26.920
of a surprise vehicle tailored to that market.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.840
India is fascinating because it's enormous price conscious

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.920
and already has strong local competition

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.660
from companies that understand

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.840
the local charging infrastructure challenges

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.240
and buyer priorities.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.680
For Tesla, this feels like a serious attempt

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:44.400
to crack a market that could eventually be massive.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:47.180
The timing suggests they've done enough homework

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.860
on pricing, local incentives,

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:52.380
and what features actually matter to Indian buyers.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.560
If they can hit the right balance between accessibility

00:04:56.120 --> 00:04:58.780
and the technology that makes a Tesla feel like a Tesla,

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:01.580
this could open the door, not just in India,

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:03.980
but set a template for other emerging markets.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.700
Customers there are going to be watching closely.

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:09.460
Some will be excited about the brand finally arriving.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.880
Others will be skeptical until they see real world range

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:15.900
in 40 degree heat with the AC blasting.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.080
Early reception on April 22nd and the weeks after

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.420
could tell us a lot about how Tesla approaches

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.740
these price-sensitive regions going forward.

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:26.560
While the company is pushing into new territory,

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.520
it's also quietly closing a chapter

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.800
on some of its very first flagships.

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.700
Tesla is marking the end of the signature series

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:35.320
for the Model S and Model X.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:38.280
Those limited run early cars were the ones

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.920
that helped establish the brand's premium reputation.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.820
The ones early adopters bought when Tesla was still

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:46.140
very much the underdog trying to prove EVs

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.080
could be desirable.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.840
Saying goodbye to that chapter feels symbolic.

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:52.820
It's a transition toward updated versions of SNX,

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.520
but also a sharper focus on higher volume models

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.480
and the newer platforms that are coming.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.480
For long-time owners who bought those signature cars,

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:02.700
it probably feels a bit like the end of an era.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.200
Those vehicles literally put Tesla on the map.

00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.680
At the same time, the move reflects how the product lineup

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:09.500
keeps evolving.

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.340
Tesla has always been willing to phase things out

00:06:12.340 --> 00:06:15.160
once the technology and cost structure have moved on.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:17.820
It's a reminder that even the halo cars

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.760
eventually become legacy products

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:22.900
as the company tries to make electric driving accessible

00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:25.840
to more people rather than just the early enthusiasts.

00:06:26.380 --> 00:06:28.260
From those legacy flagships,

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.840
we swing straight into the future ones.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:33.680
More than 50 cybercabs have been spotted

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.480
parked outside Giga, Texas.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
Some of the units look like they've already been

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.740
through crash testing, which tells you

00:06:39.740 --> 00:06:42.980
the validation work is intensifying ahead of the public launch.

00:06:43.500 --> 00:06:47.080
Seeing that many dedicated robotaxi vehicles in one place

00:06:47.080 --> 00:06:49.540
makes the whole program feel a lot more real.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.220
This isn't just renderings or a single prototype anymore.

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:56.300
It's tangible metal and glass going through the brutal testing

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.900
that autonomous vehicles need

00:06:57.900 --> 00:06:59.880
before they can be trusted at scale.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.500
For Tesla's broader autonomous ambitions,

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:03.660
this is encouraging.

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:06.420
The CyberCab represents a clean sheet design

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.180
built from the ground up for unsupervised operation.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:13.320
No steering wheel, simpler interior, lower cost structure.

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:15.640
The fact they're already stacking them

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.940
and smashing them in tests suggests

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:20.160
the engineering team is methodically checking

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.100
the boxes on safety and durability.

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.940
Of course, the gap between we have 50

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:26.300
that survive crash tests

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:29.260
and we have thousands operating safely on public roads

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:30.500
is still enormous.

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:33.100
But directionally, it feels like progress

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:35.440
on the dedicated robotaxi platform

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.460
that Elon has been talking about for years.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.140
That push into robotaxis is part of a bigger story

00:07:41.140 --> 00:07:43.120
about staying ahead in the US market.

00:07:43.820 --> 00:07:47.340
Tesla continues to outsell its major domestic EV competitors,

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.800
GM Ford, Rivian, you name it.

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.700
Those numbers have prompted Elon Musk to push back

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.820
pretty directly against the recurring narrative

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.220
that Tesla killers are about to arrive.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.240
The sales leadership still matters

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.260
because it reflects real world demand

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:02.560
and the brand strength

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:03.960
that at least in North America

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.820
continues to set Tesla apart.

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:09.540
Execution on deliveries, consistent software updates

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:12.760
and the supercharger network still give the company an edge

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:14.200
that traditional players are finding

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:16.020
surprisingly difficult to replicate.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:17.500
It's worth being clear-eyed though.

00:08:17.940 --> 00:08:19.420
Competition is intensifying

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.640
and some of those legacy automakers

00:08:21.640 --> 00:08:23.580
are finally getting better at EVs.

00:08:23.880 --> 00:08:25.340
But the gap in actual sales,

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.840
especially when you look at vehicles

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:29.120
that are truly competitive on price and range,

00:08:29.660 --> 00:08:31.220
still tilts heavily toward Tesla.

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:34.220
That domestic strength provides a solid foundation

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:36.840
while the company works through the harder challenges

00:08:36.840 --> 00:08:40.360
of regulatory approval and scaling unsupervised

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:41.780
driving in multiple countries.

00:08:42.180 --> 00:08:43.440
And while all this is happening

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.100
on the sales and regulatory front,

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.860
existing owners are getting a nice refresh this spring.

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.720
The spring 2026 software update

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:52.780
is bringing roughly 12 new features

00:08:52.780 --> 00:08:54.320
that people have been asking for.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.360
The redesigned self-driving app tailored specifically

00:08:57.360 --> 00:09:00.260
for AI4 hardware looks cleaner and more intuitive.

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:03.680
There's the enhanced voice, AI we talked about earlier,

00:09:03.860 --> 00:09:07.000
better safety lighting logic, pet display customization,

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:10.100
one tap, FSD subscription options

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.400
and a bunch of smaller quality of life tweaks.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.100
The centerpiece for many

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:15.620
will be the more thoughtful interface

00:09:15.620 --> 00:09:17.280
for full self-driving controls.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.840
It just feels less buried in menus now.

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:21.780
What continues to impress me

00:09:21.780 --> 00:09:23.240
is how these over-the-air updates

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:25.000
keep adding meaningful value years

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.380
after someone buys the car.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.700
Most automakers still treat software

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:30.180
as something you get at delivery

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.860
and then maybe patch occasionally.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:34.020
Tesla treats the car like a product

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.180
that improves over time.

00:09:35.460 --> 00:09:38.040
For owners that's become one of the biggest retention features,

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:39.660
your car literally gets better

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.860
while it sits in the driveway.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:44.000
That ongoing improvement also ties directly

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.080
into the economic argument for going electric.

00:09:46.560 --> 00:09:50.300
I saw one owner report spending only about $2,300

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:53.020
on electricity and maintenance over 50,000 miles.

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.120
That's the kind of number that makes you stop

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:57.320
and do the math on what the equivalent gasoline

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.620
and service bills would have been.

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.440
For anyone driving a decent amount each year,

00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:02.960
the lower operating costs

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:05.100
are where the EV advantage really shows up

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.000
once you get past the initial purchase price.

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:09.600
Real-world data like this helps cut through

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.380
a lot of the lingering skepticism

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:12.860
about total cost of ownership.

00:10:13.300 --> 00:10:15.560
It's one thing to read glossy brochure numbers.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.520
It's another to see someone put actual miles on a car

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:19.500
and show the receipts.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.160
That kind of practical evidence

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.260
is part of why some longtime EV reviewers

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:27.180
are getting vocal about buyers still choosing the wrong cars.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.180
One writer who has tested pretty much every major EV

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:33.260
on the market, Tesla, Rivian, the legacy brands,

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.880
recently argued that a lot of American buyers

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:38.060
are still prioritizing brand, size,

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.840
or marketing over efficiency, software experience,

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:42.140
and long-term reliability.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.880
The piece isn't a blind Tesla love letter.

00:10:45.340 --> 00:10:47.180
It's more of a plea to look at actual needs

00:10:47.180 --> 00:10:48.740
in the current state of technology

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:50.600
rather than just what the billboard says.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:53.540
For the broader industry, it raises an interesting question.

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:55.620
Are purchase decisions being driven

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:58.580
by real-world performance or by who spends the most

00:10:58.580 --> 00:10:59.500
on advertising?

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.920
Tesla owners will probably not along

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.100
at the parts that highlight efficiency and continuous updates,

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:07.800
but the review is also a useful gut check.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.880
Not every buyer needs the same thing

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:12.380
and sometimes the biggest flashiest SUV

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.720
isn't actually the smartest long-term choice

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:16.520
for how someone really uses a car.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:18.860
On a lighter note, I got a kick out

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:21.540
of a casual cyber cab sighting in Naples, Florida.

00:11:22.060 --> 00:11:23.780
Some regular person was driving along,

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:25.440
noticed this unusual vehicle,

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.700
and only realized after the fact that it was a cyber cab

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:32.080
heading toward the local Tesla delivery center.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:35.960
These everyday encounters are starting to happen more often,

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:39.240
not just at big events or on Elon's Twitter feed,

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:41.240
but in ordinary towns where people

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:42.760
are just going about their day.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:46.920
The community reaction is usually a fun mix of,

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:49.600
wait, was that real and genuine excitement?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:51.060
It's a small thing,

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.900
but it humanizes the Robotaxi program

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:56.000
and makes the future feel a little closer

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.380
than it did six months ago.

00:11:58.220 --> 00:12:01.220
On the financial side, UBS upgraded its rating on Tesla,

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:04.240
pointing to the long-term upside in AI and autonomy.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:07.700
The bank basically said that while near-term challenges

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:10.020
around margins and competition still exist,

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:12.360
the potential in software and Robotaxis

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.200
is starting to look big enough to justify more optimism.

00:12:15.640 --> 00:12:18.500
It's a notable shift in tone from a major Wall Streethouse

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.500
and you can tell investors are paying attention

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:22.440
because the stock reacted accordingly.

00:12:22.920 --> 00:12:26.060
Whether those AI valuations ultimately prove accurate

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:27.180
is still up for debate,

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:29.100
but it's another sign that the conversation

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:31.940
is moving beyond just quarterly vehicle deliveries.

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:34.820
Of course, not everyone is waving pom-poms.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.440
Gary Black described the recent full self-driving

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:39.840
approval in Europe as essentially a non-event.

00:12:40.340 --> 00:12:42.420
His point, and I think it's a fair one,

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.100
is that regulatory clearance by itself

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:47.640
doesn't automatically translate into revenue

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:48.900
or widespread adoption.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.820
You still need the technology to perform consistently

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:54.300
at a high level across wildly different conditions,

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:56.100
traffic cultures and road rules.

00:12:56.700 --> 00:12:59.360
Europe's diversity makes that harder than it looks on paper.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:01.740
The contrast between the UBS upgrade

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.780
and Gary Black's grounded take is healthy.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.440
It keeps the autonomy conversation

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:06.660
from getting too frothy.

00:13:07.040 --> 00:13:09.740
Tesla has positioned itself well to close that gap

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:11.100
with its vision-based system

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:12.740
and rapid over-the-air iteration,

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.100
but honest execution will matter far more

00:13:15.100 --> 00:13:16.220
than any single headline.

00:13:16.220 --> 00:13:19.960
The next 12 to 18 months of real-world unsupervised miles

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.340
are going to be more important than any approval letter.

00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.120
Before we wrap up,

00:13:24.440 --> 00:13:25.720
it's worth taking a step back

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.660
and applying a bit of first principles thinking

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.860
to what actually makes a smaller, more affordable,

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.840
Tesla viable in markets like India.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.260
The popular assumption is that you have

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.440
to heavily compromise range or features

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:38.540
to hit a aggressive price point.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:41.000
But if you break it down to fundamentals,

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:45.060
energy density, structural battery integration,

00:13:45.660 --> 00:13:47.460
cell manufacturing improvements,

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.100
and the leverage that software provides,

00:13:50.480 --> 00:13:51.520
the picture changes.

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.060
We saw with early Model 3 production

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.440
how pairing a smaller battery with high-efficiency motors,

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.600
good aerodynamics and minimal hardware changes

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.900
can still deliver meaningful, real-world utility.

00:14:04.520 --> 00:14:08.800
A vehicle using roughly 60 to 70% of the battery capacity

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:11.320
of a Model Y could still give you highway range

00:14:11.320 --> 00:14:14.500
that's perfectly usable for most Indian city-to-city trips

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:16.500
while costing thousands less to build

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:17.840
at mature factory yields.

00:14:18.500 --> 00:14:21.140
The real trick is that most of the customer value

00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:23.460
after purchase comes from software updates

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.660
rather than added physical parts.

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:28.800
Efficiency modes, navigation optimizations,

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.580
thermal management improvements,

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.980
all of those can be delivered over the air

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.560
and keep the car feeling fresh,

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:36.900
even if the battery pack is smaller on paper.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:39.280
A truly affordable Tesla doesn't need

00:14:39.280 --> 00:14:41.240
to win on every raw specification.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.340
It needs to be the vehicle where cost per mile

00:14:44.340 --> 00:14:47.520
falls fastest and where the ownership experience stays

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:50.060
ahead of competitors through continuous improvement.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.840
Getting that balance right in India

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.200
could be a blueprint for other emerging markets

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.080
where legacy automakers have struggled

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.340
to make money for decades.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.680
So yeah, I'll be watching customer feedback

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:02.720
after the April 22nd event pretty closely.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.860
It could shape Tesla's approach

00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:06.060
for the next couple of years.

